{"name":"Zindalankh","status":"ok","title":"Zindalankh","pageId":55291,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Zindalankh</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TH.VI-p41_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VI-p41-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">City</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Murgh%C3%B4m\" title=\"Murghôm\">Murghôm</a>, the <a href=\"/wiki/Hordelands\" title=\"Hordelands\">Hordelands</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a class=\"newcategory\" href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Zindalankh\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Zindalankh\">Inhabitants of  Zindalankh</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2F0ZWdvcnk6TG9jYXRpb25zX2luX1ppbmRhbGFua2g/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\" title=\"Category:Locations in Zindalankh (page does not exist)\">Locations in  Zindalankh</span></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ2F0ZWdvcnk6T3JnYW5pemF0aW9uc19pbl9aaW5kYWxhbmtoP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Zindalankh (page does not exist)\">Organizations in  Zindalankh</span></nav>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Zindalankh</b> was a coastal city of <a href=\"/wiki/Murgh%C3%B4m\" title=\"Murghôm\">Murghôm</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TH.VI-p41_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VI-p41-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Location\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Location</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Background\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Background</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Notable_Inhabitants\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Inhabitants</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Location\">Location</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Location\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Zindalankh?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Location\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Zindalankh sat on the western rim of the <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvU2VtcGhhcl9XYXRlcj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Semphar Water (page does not exist)\">Semphar Water</span> within the southern portion of <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Brightstar_Lake\" title=\"Brightstar Lake\">Gbor Nor</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TH.VI-p41_1-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VI-p41-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Background\">Background</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Background\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Zindalankh?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Background\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Zindalankh hosted a <a href=\"/wiki/Shou\" title=\"Shou\">Shou</a> Town.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Zindalankh?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Around the <a href=\"/wiki/350_DR\" title=\"350 DR\">Year of the Hunter, 350 DR</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Martek\" title=\"Martek\">Martek</a> departed from the city in a caravan headed for <a href=\"/wiki/Medinat_Muskawoon\" title=\"Medinat Muskawoon\">Medinat Muskawoon</a> with the intention of stopping <a href=\"/wiki/Khalitharius\" title=\"Khalitharius\">Khalitharius</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DoD-p93_3-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DoD-p93-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Zindalankh was a fierce rival of <a href=\"/wiki/Dhaztanar\" title=\"Dhaztanar\">Dhaztanar</a>, which was located on the opposite bank of the Semphar Water in <a href=\"/wiki/Semphar\" title=\"Semphar\">Semphar</a>. Being located at the end of the <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUm9hZF9vZl90aGVfRGF3bj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Road of the Dawn (page does not exist)\">Road of the Dawn</span>, it controlled trade to the west, just as Dhaztanar controlled trade to the east, and both cities vied for control over the trade in Gbor Nor.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TH.VII-p109_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VII-p109-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Ultimately, Dhaztanar won the power struggle by lobbying to make the <a href=\"/wiki/River_Rauthenflow\" title=\"River Rauthenflow\">River Rauthenflow</a> navigable by boats, allowing people to bypass Zindalankh, and sail straight from the <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Inner_Sea\" title=\"Inner Sea\">Inner Sea</a> to Dhaztanar's docks, destroying the city's power.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TH.VII-p109_4-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VII-p109-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>By <a href=\"/wiki/1359_DR\" title=\"1359 DR\">1359 DR</a>, Zindalankh had shrunk. Its fortunes were gone and its people were poor and destitute. The city became a haven for the pirates of Gbor Nor. People came to the city to sell stolen items, and buy others for far less than their value. Thievery, and the sword, were the only law.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TH.VII-p109_4-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VII-p109-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Though officially under the rule of the <a href=\"/wiki/Bey\" title=\"Bey\">Bey</a> of Murghôm, few followed his laws, and only tolerated him for the protection he gave to the city. Were it not for the forces of Murghom stationed there, Semphar would have destroyed the city long before. However, doing so with the Bey's men there would have been seen as an act of war, something Semphar wanted to avoid.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TH.VII-p109_4-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VII-p109-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Inhabitants\">Notable Inhabitants</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Inhabitants\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Zindalankh?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Notable Inhabitants\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Ghuldribrand_Mroster\" title=\"Ghuldribrand Mroster\">Ghuldribrand Mroster</a>, Mage Royal of Zindalankh</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Zindalankh?veaction=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>A ruin in the <a href=\"/wiki/Plains_of_Purple_Dust\" title=\"Plains of Purple Dust\">Plains of Purple Dust</a> southwest of Zindalankh held the process which <a href=\"/wiki/Velsharoon\" title=\"Velsharoon\">Velsharoon</a> used to become a <a href=\"/wiki/Lich\" title=\"Lich\">lich</a> and then ascend.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PnP-p77_5-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-PnP-p77-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Zindalankh?veaction=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Zindalankh?veaction=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-TH.VI-p41-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VI-p41_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VI-p41_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VI-p41_1-2\">1.2</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/David_Cook\" title=\"David Cook\">David Cook</a> (August 1990). “Volume I”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Steve_Winter\" title=\"Steve Winter\">Steve Winter</a> ed. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Horde\" title=\"The Horde\">The Horde</a></i> (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 41. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-88038-868-4\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-88038-868-4\">0-88038-868-4</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eytan_Bernstein\" title=\"Eytan Bernstein\">Eytan Bernstein</a> (2007-05-09). <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20180324222724/http://archive.wizards.com/default.asp?x=dnd/frcc/20070918\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Eastern Classes</a>. <a href=\"/wiki/Class_Chronicles\" title=\"Class Chronicles\">Class Chronicles</a>. <a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>. Archived from <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://archive.wizards.com/default.asp?x=dnd/frcc/20070918\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">the original</a> on 2018-03-24. Retrieved on 2016-05-21.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-DoD-p93-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-DoD-p93_3-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Tracy_Hickman\" title=\"Tracy Hickman\">Tracy Hickman</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Laura_Hickman\" title=\"Laura Hickman\">Laura Hickman</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Philip_Meyers\" title=\"Philip Meyers\">Philip Meyers</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Peter_Rice\" title=\"Peter Rice\">Peter Rice</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/William_John_Wheeler\" title=\"William John Wheeler\">William John Wheeler</a> (May 1987). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Desert_of_Desolation\" title=\"Desert of Desolation\">Desert of Desolation</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 93. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0880383974\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0880383974\">978-0880383974</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-TH.VII-p109-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VII-p109_4-0\">4.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VII-p109_4-1\">4.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VII-p109_4-2\">4.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VII-p109_4-3\">4.3</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/David_Cook\" title=\"David Cook\">David Cook</a> (August 1990). “Volume II”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Steve_Winter\" title=\"Steve Winter\">Steve Winter</a> ed. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Horde\" title=\"The Horde\">The Horde</a></i> (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 109. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-88038-868-4\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-88038-868-4\">0-88038-868-4</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-PnP-p77-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-PnP-p77_5-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eric_L._Boyd\" title=\"Eric L. Boyd\">Eric L. Boyd</a> (September 1997). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Powers_%26_Pantheons\" title=\"Powers &amp; Pantheons\">Powers &amp; Pantheons</a></i>. Edited by <a href=\"/wiki/Julia_Martin\" title=\"Julia Martin\">Julia Martin</a>. (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 77. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0786906574\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0786906574\">978-0786906574</a>.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260517010919\nCache expiry: 1209600\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.100 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.184 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1508/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 6760/2097152 bytes\nTem